• different employee/employer relationships and the existence of works councils and labor unions;
• compliance with the U.S.Foreign Corrupt Practices Act and other applicable U.S.and foreign laws prohibiting
corrupt payments to government officials and other third parties;
• laws and policies of the U.S.and other jurisdictions affecting trade,foreign investment,loans,andtaxes;and
• geopolitical events,including war and terrorism.
As international physical,e-commerce,and omni channel retail and other services grow,competition will intensify,
including through adoption of evolving business models.Local companies may have a substantial competitive advantage
because of their greater understanding of,andfocuson,the local customer,as well as their more established local brand names.
